yezhihao/jt808-server — Apache License, Version 2.0
https://github.com/yezhihao/jt808-server
https://gitee.com/yezhihao/jt808-server
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The JT/T 808, JT/T 1078 and T/JSATL12 protocol model, codecs and parts of the
signalling endpoints are derived from this project. The code retains its
original package namespace `org.yzh.**` and most files keep the upstream
author header. Affected locations:

  jt-platform/jt-common/src/main/java/org/yzh/commons/**
  jt-platform/jt-protocol/src/main/java/org/yzh/protocol/**
  jt-platform/jt-signal/src/main/java/org/yzh/web/**
  (and the corresponding src/test trees)

Copyright remains with yezhihao and the upstream contributors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
jt1078service / jt1078-stream-server — MIT License
https://gitee.com/lxygit0731/jt1078-stream-server
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The JT/T 1078 media ingest, stream distribution, talkback and recording
behaviour in `jt-platform/jt-media` was rewritten from this project into the
`io.github.jtplatform.media.**` namespace. The browser player SDK in
`packages/jt-player` was likewise refactored from its raw-stream player
implementation.

Copyright remains with the original jt1078service contributors.
See jt-platform/LICENSE-MIT and packages/jt-player/LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
soybeanjs/soybean-admin v2.2.0 — MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 Soybean
https://github.com/soybeanjs/soybean-admin
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The administration console in `jt-console-ui` is a fork of SoybeanAdmin
v2.2.0. The layout system, theme engine, routing conventions, request layer
and the internal `@sa/*` workspace packages all originate from that project;
this repository adds the fleet monitoring, vehicle, geofence, alarm and track
playback screens on top of it.

The upstream MIT license text is retained verbatim at jt-console-ui/LICENSE.

